+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+On the adversarial synthetic vocabulary of 30 frequent words, the measured p95
+for the full-recall `UserPromptSubmit` hook was **10.27 ms** before the
+term-selection fix.
+
+The fix made term selection discard terms whose document frequency is greater
+than one third of the active store (`df > n / 3`). Such terms carry little
+discriminating information while producing long FTS posting-list scans. The
+selector still ranks the remaining terms by IDF and keeps the top eight.
+
+The measured full-recall p95 after that change was **1.82 ms**. The recorded
+post-fix benchmark also changed the synthetic generator from the adversarial
+30-word-only vocabulary to a Zipf-distributed vocabulary (30 frequent domain
+words plus rare identifiers), so the before/after figures are historical hook
+measurements, not a controlled comparison with an otherwise identical corpus.
